1
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:10,160
Machan, my throat really hurts, da.
Feels like a fever too.

2
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:13,036
What happened, da?
Shall we go to the doctor?

3
00:00:13,116 --> 00:00:16,942
No need for all that, da.
Let's ask ChatGPT.

4
00:00:20,984 --> 00:00:25,144
Da, I had the same thing before.
I took Amoxicillin.

5
00:00:25,224 --> 00:00:26,824
You can take it too, da!

6
00:00:26,904 --> 00:00:29,950
OK da! Come, let's go to the pharmacy!

7
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:33,427
♪ If you've got a body for injections… ♪

8
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:36,327
♪ Do we really need to see a doctor? ♪

9
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:39,200
♪ Let's cycle to the pharmacy… ♪

10
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:42,677
♪ Shall we just buy some pills and pop them? ♪

11
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:51,036
Anna, do you have Amoxicillin?
I have a sore throat and fever.

12
00:00:52,081 --> 00:00:55,005
See, da! We got the tablets so easily!

13
00:00:55,085 --> 00:00:58,430
Yeah, da! Come, let's go home!

14
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:06,585
Hey… you foolish humans!
Can't you think even a little?

15
00:01:06,665 --> 00:01:09,820
Sore throat? Antibiotic!
Fever? Antibiotic!

16
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:13,009
You pop pills without even knowing
why you're taking them!

17
00:01:13,089 --> 00:01:16,052
Don't you know antibiotics
don't work against viruses?

18
00:01:16,132 --> 00:01:18,252
You even harm the good bacteria
that protect you!

19
00:01:18,332 --> 00:01:22,325
You think you're destroying us…
but some of us survive and multiply!

20
00:01:22,405 --> 00:01:24,816
Ha ha ha! We survive and multiply!

21
00:01:24,896 --> 00:01:29,777
When the medicines that can fight us run out…
who's going to stop our game, eh?

22
00:01:29,857 --> 00:01:31,566
This is what you call
Antimicrobial Resistance!

23
00:01:31,646 --> 00:01:35,092
When medicines stop working for some infections,
what will you do?

24
00:01:35,172 --> 00:01:39,950
Unnecessary antibiotic use allows
resistant bacteria to survive and multiply.

25
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:47,221
Doctor, the fever hasn't come down at all.
He's really unwell now!

26
00:01:47,301 --> 00:01:52,802
Alright, please don't worry. We'll examine him
and do the necessary investigations.

27
00:01:52,882 --> 00:01:54,950
Finding the cause of the infection
is important.

28
00:01:57,600 --> 00:02:01,735
Doctor, the culture report shows this bacterium
is resistant to many antibiotics.

29
00:02:01,815 --> 00:02:05,483
It's important to choose treatment
based on the susceptibility results.

30
00:02:05,563 --> 00:02:11,237
Alright. We'll decide the right treatment based on
the patient's clinical condition and the report.

31
00:02:11,481 --> 00:02:13,800
Antibiotics are not the answer
to every illness.

32
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:17,753
A sore throat or fever doesn't mean
you automatically need an antibiotic.

33
00:02:17,833 --> 00:02:23,889
Many infections are caused by viruses;
antibiotics don't work against viruses.

34
00:02:23,969 --> 00:02:27,750
Antimicrobial resistance is not resistance
that develops in humans;

35
00:02:27,830 --> 00:02:29,888
it's the bacteria that gain
the ability to resist antibiotics.

36
00:02:29,968 --> 00:02:34,950
Unnecessary and incorrect antibiotic use
can make this problem worse.

37
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:39,428
Don't take antibiotics
without a doctor's advice.

38
00:02:39,508 --> 00:02:42,160
Follow the prescribed dose and duration.

39
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:44,742
Using antibiotics responsibly
is the duty of every one of us.

40
00:02:44,822 --> 00:02:48,379
They must keep helping to save lives,
today and tomorrow.

41
00:02:48,459 --> 00:02:55,878
USE ANTIBIOTICS WISELY.
STOP ANTIMICROBIAL RESISTANCE. SAVE OUR FUTURE!
